# NEXA App - Theme & Styling Guide

## Source of Truth

Colors are defined as `@theme` CSS custom properties in `App.css`. Tailwind auto-generates semantic utility classes from them (`bg-nexa`, `text-healthy`, `border-critical`, etc.).

For programmatic contexts (Recharts fills, Google Maps styles, inline SVG strokes), import from `config/nexaColors.js` — it mirrors the `@theme` tokens exactly.

**Do NOT hardcode hex values in JSX.** Use Tailwind theme utilities or `nexaColors` imports.

## Primitives (use these, don't re-roll)

Reusable UI primitives live in `frontend/src/components/ui/`. Prefer them over re-implementing markup:

- **`Button`** (+ `buttonVariants`) — variants `primary/secondary/subtle/danger/ghost` × sizes `sm/md/lg`. Never inline `backgroundColor` + `onMouseEnter`/`onMouseLeave` hover swaps.
- **`Input`** — token focus (`focus:border-nexa`), 16px text, `error` state. Never `style.borderColor` focus/blur handlers.
- **`Badge`** — status pill with a `tone` prop (neutral/healthy/critical/warning/info/resting); tones live in `lib/statusStyles.js`.
- **`Card`** — standard white-panel chrome (`border rounded-xl shadow-sm`, padding variants, optional hover elevation).
- **`SearchField`** + `filters/FilterButton` + `common/ExportCsvButton` — the shared list-page toolbar atoms.

The full rollout, decisions, and deferred work live in `docs/development/FRONTEND_STANDARDIZATION.md` — the authoritative reference for the consumer design system.

## Color Palette

### Primary Colors
- **Nexa (neutral green)**: `bg-nexa` / `text-nexa` / `border-nexa` (`#4a6b5f`)
- **Nexa Hover**: `hover:bg-nexa-hover` (`#5A7B6F`)
- **Nexa Light**: `bg-nexa-light` (`rgba(74, 107, 95, 0.15)`)

### Health Status
- **Healthy**: `text-healthy` / `bg-healthy` (`#4C9A14`)
- **Healthy Hover**: `hover:bg-healthy-hover` (`#3d7b10`)
- **Healthy Background**: `bg-healthy-bg` (`#eafbe3`)
- **Healthy Soft**: `text-healthy-soft` (`#7aaf6f`) — softer green for links, map markers, chart lines
- **Healthy Light**: `bg-healthy-light` (`#ECFDF5`)

### Alert/Status Colors
- **Critical**: `bg-critical` / `text-critical` (`#EF4444`)
- **Critical Hover**: `hover:bg-critical-hover` (`#dc2626`)
- **Critical Background**: `bg-critical-bg` (`#FEE2E2`)
- **Critical Text**: `text-critical-text` (`#991B1B`)
- **Warning**: `bg-warning` / `text-warning` (`#F59E0B`)
- **Warning Background**: `bg-warning-bg` (`#ffee8c`)
- **Warning Text**: `text-warning-text` (`#9A3412`)
- **Info**: `bg-info` / `text-info` (`#2563eb`)
- **Info Background**: `bg-info-bg` (`#dbeafe`)
- **Info Text**: `text-info-text` (`#1e40af`)

### Movement Colors (behavior, not health)
Movement chips deliberately sit outside the health greens and the estrus
blue/purple family so no chip hue is shared across the three status domains.
- **Active**: `text-active` (`#1F7A70`) on `bg-active-bg` (`#DDF2EF`) — kinetic teal, neutral not positive
- **Resting**: `bg-resting` (`#8FA6C4`, used at `/25`) with `text-resting-dark` (`#44618B`) — calm steel blue

### Estrus Phase Colors
- **Breed Now**: `bg-info-bg text-info-text`
- **Closing**: `bg-estrus-closing/25` (`#A47DAB`) with `text-estrus-closing-dark` (`#7A4D8A`)
- **Missed**: `bg-gray-100 text-gray-500`

### Secondary Colors
- **Chart Accent**: `nexaColors.chartAccent` (`#8884d8`)

### Neutral Colors
- Use Tailwind's built-in `gray-*` scale for text, borders, and backgrounds.

## Component Patterns

### Buttons
Use the `ui/Button` primitive; its `variant` maps to these tokens:
- **primary**: `bg-nexa text-white hover:bg-nexa-hover`
- **secondary** (outline): `bg-white text-gray-700 border-2 border-gray-200 hover:bg-gray-50`
- **subtle** (gray): `bg-gray-100 text-gray-700 hover:bg-gray-200`
- **danger**: `bg-critical text-white hover:bg-critical-hover`
- **ghost**: `text-gray-600 hover:text-gray-900 hover:bg-gray-50`
- **Sizes** `sm`/`md`/`lg`; geometry `rounded-lg text-sm font-medium`.

### Status Badges
Use the `ui/Badge` primitive (`tone` prop) with the `lib/statusStyles.js` tone maps. Tones map to these token pairs:
```javascript
healthy:  'bg-healthy-bg text-healthy'             // Healthy
critical: 'bg-critical-bg text-critical-text'       // Sick
warning:  'bg-warning-bg-strong text-warning-text'  // At Risk
active:   'bg-active-bg text-active'                // Active (movement)
resting:  'bg-resting/25 text-resting-dark'         // Resting (movement)
neutral:  'bg-gray-100 text-gray-800'
```
Never `bg-orange-200` / `bg-red-200` for status.

### Cards
Use the `ui/Card` primitive (`padding` + `interactive` props). It renders:
- `bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl shadow-sm p-4 md:p-6`
- Interactive: `hover:shadow-md transition-all duration-300`

### Charts & Data Visualization
- Primary data line: `nexaColors.nexa`
- Grid lines: `nexaColors.gray50`
- Target/reference lines: `nexaColors.gray400` (dashed)
- Data points: `nexaColors.nexa` fill, white stroke

### Map Markers
- Healthy: `nexaColors.healthySoft`
- At Risk: `nexaColors.warning`
- Sick: `nexaColors.critical`
- Border: white stroke, strokeWeight: 2

## Loading States

### Data pages — hand-written `animate-pulse` skeletons
Each data page has a loading guard that shows pulse skeleton markup matching the page layout (title bars, stat cards, table rows, etc.). Keep skeletons in sync with layout changes.

### Patterns that are intentionally different
- **Auth form buttons**: text swap ("Signing in...") — instant feedback on the clicked element
- **Chatbot messages**: custom LoadingIndicator typing dots — chat UX convention
- **App-level initial load**: full-screen PageLoader (Lottie) — one-time branding moment
- **Inline form submit**: button text swap or inline spinner

## Empty States

Use the `<EmptyState />` component for all "no data" scenarios. No red error styling for missing data.

```jsx
import EmptyState from '../components/common/EmptyState'

<EmptyState
  icon={<SomeIcon className="w-16 h-16" />}
  title="No items found"
  subtitle="Try adjusting your search or filters."
  action={<Button onClick={...}>Clear filters</Button>}
/>
```

## Error Handling

### Page-level data fetch errors
- **Blocking** (can't render without data): centered error + retry (AppLayout's ranch error pattern)
- **Non-blocking** (partial failure): `<ErrorBanner message={error} onRetry={retry} />`

### Form validation
- Inline `text-sm text-red-600` beneath the field — keep as-is

### Do NOT
- Use `alert()` or `window.alert()`
- Silently swallow errors (log-only with no UI feedback)
- Set error state without rendering it

## Typography
- **Headings**: `font-bold text-gray-900` — h1: `text-2xl md:text-3xl`, h2: `text-xl md:text-2xl`, h3: `text-lg md:text-xl`
- **Body**: `text-sm md:text-base text-gray-700`
- **Small**: `text-xs text-gray-500`
- **Font**: Instrument Sans (default), Google Sans (chatbot), JetBrains Mono (data)

## Spacing
- Page padding: `p-6 md:p-8`
- Section spacing: `space-y-6`
- Card spacing: `gap-4`

## Responsive Breakpoints
- Mobile: < 640px (`sm:`)
- Tablet: 640px - 1024px (`md:`)
- Desktop: > 1024px (`lg:`, `xl:`)

## Responsive & Mobile Rules
- **Base classes are the phone layer** (mobile-first); `sm:` (640px) is the first step up. There is no `xs` breakpoint — do not use `xs:` variants.
- **Tables**: every `<table>` renders inside a scroll shell with an explicit min content width (internal app: `ui/TableShell`) so narrow viewports scroll horizontally instead of compressing columns; add a bounded `max-h` + `overflow-y-auto` once a list can exceed ~10 rows. Never a bare `w-full` table in an `overflow-x-auto` div.
- **Overlays**: fixed panels/dropdowns/modals cap to the viewport (`max-w-[calc(100vw-…)]`, `max-h-[85dvh]`) and scroll internally; portaled menus clamp/flip at the edges; modals lock body scroll while open.
- **Toolbars**: control rows (buttons, pills, tabs, filters) wrap or stack below `sm`; no fixed-width control may force horizontal page scroll.
- **Viewport units**: use `dvh` (`h-dvh`, `min-h-dvh`, `max-h-[85dvh]`), never `vh`/`h-screen` — iOS browser chrome shrinks `vh`.
- **JS breakpoints**: use the `useResponsive` hook (`isMobile` = <768 for nav/chrome); never hardcode new `window.innerWidth` comparisons.
- **Touch**: no hover-only affordances — anything revealed by `group-hover` must be visible or reachable below `sm`.
- Form controls render at 16px below `sm` (global CSS rule in both apps) so iOS Safari does not zoom on focus; do not design sub-16px mobile inputs.

## Forms
- Use the `ui/Input` primitive: `border-2 border-gray-200 focus:border-nexa`, 16px text, `error` prop for the invalid state. No imperative `style.borderColor` focus/blur handlers.
- Label: `text-sm font-medium text-gray-700`
- Error: `text-sm text-red-600`
